  "source": ["state[i] = r[i+1] for i = 0..7;", "repeat 4 times: choose one right operand per lane, then shuffle the lane update order;", "for each (left, right) in that order: next.append(state[left] + state[right]);", "state = next; each old lane is used at least once as a left operand;", "write state[i] to r[i+10] for i = 0..7;", "The concrete right operands and order are the literal lhs/rhs edges in ir."],
